	(text_box "Revers polarity protection.\n\nWhen polarity is correct,\nthe gate of the p-mos will \nget pulled to GND through R1\nand turn on the fet."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 41.148 21.844 0)
		(size 13.208 7.112)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 0.635 0.635)
				(italic yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "393593f6-d7e8-404b-ba37-ee3f2b41b43d")
	)
	(text_box "ESP32-S3-WROOM-1x\n\n*In module variants that have embedded OSPI PSRAM, i.e., that embed ESP32-S3R8, pins IO35, IO36 and IO37 are connected to the OSPI PSRAM and are not available for other uses.\n\nNote:\nESP32-S3 has four strapping pins: GPIO0, GPIO3, GPIO45 and GPIO46.\n\nGPIO0, GPIO45 and GPIO46 are connected to the chip's internal weak pull-up/pull-down during the chip reset.\n\nGPIO3 is floating by default."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 304.419 101.6 0)
		(size 30.48 33.02)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "41244bd3-ca0f-4b81-82c4-80e1784cabf2")
	)
	(text_box "PMOS VGS clamp.\n\nD2 limits the PMOS gate-source voltage\nto about -12 V.\n\nR5 pulls the gate low to turn Q1 on during\ncorrect polarity, while D2 prevents VGS from\nexceeding the MOSFET gate rating.\n\nThis zener only protects the PMOS gate.\nInput surges are handled by the TVS diode."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 63.246 48.514 0)
		(size 19.05 12.446)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 0.635 0.635)
				(italic yes)
			)
			(justify right top)
		)
		(uuid "c708da1e-c9b7-4be9-b561-31e74621cca6")
	)
	(text_box "Surge protection.\n\nTransients will get pulled to GND"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 24.892 50.546 0)
		(size 14.478 3.81)
		(stroke
